Q: How to return inserted data in typeorm and nest.js A: <p><code>.insert(event)</code> does not return the saved event, it returns an <code>InsertResult</code>. Calling <code>.save(event)</code> will return the saved object, and you can return that.</p>
<p>E.g.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>
const savedEvent = this.eventRepository.save(event);
return savedEvent;
</code></pre>
